1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:24,485
Monday morning, the day after the beach show. The inbox already knows. Megan's final count — eight hundred forty seven shells, zero incidents. The councilman who filed a noise complaint in January is suddenly asking about next year. Even the insurance man wants a word — a pleasant one, for once. And Fiona says the warehouse is empty. One company, one inbox.

2
00:00:29,485 --> 00:00:45,805
Every BoomClaw thread lives here — suppliers, permits, catering, one very persistent councilman. Three accounts on the left, one view when you want it. Unread stays honest, threads stay threads, and none of it is trapped in somebody else's cloud.

3
00:00:46,705 --> 00:01:06,716
Here's our last order, told by its own thread. The delay announcement. The panic — Valencia was four weeks out. And the resolution: McBang filled out forty seven pages of customs forms by hand, and two hundred Thunder Dragons cleared the port. The thread remembers all of it, so nobody else has to.

4
00:01:07,616 --> 00:01:24,000
Six months from now you won't remember subject lines — you'll remember a word. Customs. Search it, and the whole saga comes back… along with this morning's warning from the warehouse. Search the invoice number instead, and the paperwork finds itself.

5
00:01:25,616 --> 00:01:44,880
Now, from the chat. Ask what you'd ask a colleague: where does the Dragon Fireworks order stand? Francis reads the mail — invoice, payment, customs, cleared — and adds the part that matters today: stock is at zero, and no reorder has gone out yet. Every email he cites becomes a chip.

6
00:01:45,780 --> 00:02:02,889
So we fix that without opening a single form. Draft the reorder — two hundred chrysanthemum shells, reference the old invoice, and this time, start the customs paperwork early. Francis writes it and saves it as a draft. Not sent. You stay in charge.

7
00:02:03,789 --> 00:02:19,576
The chips are doors. Click the invoice, and you're standing in Mail, on the original thread. And in the Drafts folder, the reorder is waiting — addressed to McBang, invoice referenced, customs warning included. All it needs is your send button.

8
00:02:21,789 --> 00:02:37,362
It's all one system. The cleared-shipment email links the supplier's card, the invoice — and one more thing: the shells themselves, as an inventory item. When those two hundred shells reach the warehouse, they become part of Inventory.

9
00:02:40,089 --> 00:02:47,108
That's Mail — the paper trail of everything that goes boom, all on your own hardware. Next up: Photos.
